MID_SE_Max_Noc_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_001: Hey, you. With the face paint. What tribe are\nyou from?
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_002: "Tribe"? I don't know what you're talking about.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_003: Your face. Isn't that war paint? I noticed it back in\nthe arena.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_004: Alright... She's not onto me. She's just got the\nwrong idea.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_005: What are you mumbling about? Oh, never mind.\nListen.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_006: The place I'm from—we're often going to war with\nsome people here, some people there...
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_007: So, I've seen my share of foes who paint their\nfaces before war.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_008: I figured that's why you've got that on your face.\nWhere are you from?
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_009: Nowhere! This makeup's mine, and mine alone.\nIt ain't war paint. It's part of me!
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_010: Oh. So the "clowns" I've been seeing on the streets\nsince coming here...they're not your people?
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_011: Heh heh HEH. You tell me! They make people laugh.\nIs that what I do?
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_012: Nah—I make ME laugh. I slay my enemies and\ncackle at the sight of their blood! AHAHAHA.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_013: Hm... Don't you think this is all kinda over the top?\nI mean, that laugh is just ridiculous.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_014: Urgh... You trying to get cut? I don't recall askin'\nfor your opinion.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_015: Hey, if this is who you are, then I take it back. But\nif it's not, maybe...tone it down?
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_016: The warriors I knew who used war paint were just\nas likely to lose their nerve and run. Or die.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_017: You can't fool yourself into having more courage\nthan you do by painting yourself a new face.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_018: A-ah!
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_019: I'm not telling you what to do, but I'd hate to see\nyou die for no good reason.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_020: Some people got their own reasons for how they act...\nand can't be talked out of it.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_C_021: Fair enough. Just, you know, try not to get\nkilled, OK?
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_001: Here I go! Hyah, hah!
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_002: Whew! Nice! That was impressive.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_003: Great training session today. I love seeing the\nreal you breaking through.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_004: Thanks...but I don't really like when people call me\n"the real you." Feels weird.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_005: But the real you is...the real you. You were pushing\nyourself way too hard back in your clowning days.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_006: Wow... That bad, huh?
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_007: I was doing it for Bertrand. I put a lot of work into it.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_008: Ah, the White-Maned Demon. He's lucky to have\na friend like you.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_009: You know, I'm glad our allies and the Luminous One\nasked me to join them.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_010: The days I spent in the arena were brutal—and in all\nthe worst ways. I'd rather die than go back there.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_011: Strong words. Was it really that bad?
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_012: The gladiators I lived with were the scum of the\nearth. To put it mildly.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_013: Even the boss was a creep. I lost count of how\nmany times he hit on me.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_014: Guess it's no surprise that every guy he hired was a\nlowlife too.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_015: Eventually I got sick of it. So I slugged the boss and\ntook him out of commission for good.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_016: Uh-huh...
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_017: I was looking for a new employer when I got hired\nhere. Kinda like a mercenary, I guess.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_018: It's not a bad gig. Plenty of fights to be had, that's\nfor sure.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_019: That's an optimistic way to look at it. We're only so\nbusy because the world's in chaos...
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_020: For my part, I hope we have peace someday.\nNo more fights—no more hurting people.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_021: Ha! I always knew the real you was a softie.
MID_SE_Max_Noc_B_022: Come on... I told you I didn't like being called that.